          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            5. Is Low Calorie Protein Powder Good for Weight Loss?
          </h2>

          <p>
            It can help, for three reasons supported by research, but none of them is the powder itself. First, protein is the most filling macronutrient per calorie in most studies, so a high-protein snack tends to curb appetite better than the same calories from carbohydrate or fat. Second, protein has the highest thermic effect of food: commonly cited estimates put the energy cost of digesting it at about 20 to 30 percent of its calories, against single digits for fat and carbohydrate.
          </p>

          <p>
            Third, and most important, eating enough protein in a calorie deficit helps you keep muscle while losing fat. Reviews of dieting studies suggest higher intakes, often around 1.6 g per kilogram of body weight per day or more for people doing resistance training, protect lean mass better than lower intakes. A lean shake makes that target easier to hit without spending a large share of your calorie budget, which is the real advantage of a low-calorie powder over a richer one.
          </p>

          <p>
            What protein powder will not do is cause weight loss on its own. Adding a 110-calorie shake to an unchanged diet adds 110 calories. The benefit comes when the shake replaces something less filling, such as a pastry, a sugary coffee or an afternoon snack, or when it helps you reach a protein target that keeps hunger under control. Products marketed as fat-burning protein add stimulants or extras that do little; our <a href="/best-fat-burning-protein-powder/">fat-burning protein powder</a> guide explains why plain isolate is usually the better buy.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you are using a GLP-1 medication, eating very little, or managing diabetes, kidney disease or another condition, talk to your doctor or a registered dietitian about how much protein you need and how to get it. Our <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-glp-1/">best protein powder for GLP-1</a> guide covers that situation, and our sibling guide on <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-body-recomposition/">protein powder for body recomposition</a> covers losing fat while building muscle.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="under-150-calories" class="scroll-mt-24">
