          </h2>

          <p>
            The powder is often the smallest part of a shake's calories. A 100-calorie scoop can become a 400-calorie drink with whole milk, a banana and a spoon of peanut butter. None of those are bad foods, and a bigger shake can be a sensible meal, but if you bought a low-calorie powder to keep a snack light, the mixer and add-ins decide whether that happens. The table shows typical figures to plan around.
          </p>

